# Styling & UI Conventions

This educational project uses inline styles and CSS modules for styling. This approach prioritizes clarity and understanding over production best practices.

## Styling Approach

### Inline Styles (Educational Purpose)
This project uses inline styles extensively for educational clarity:

```typescript
// Educational component styling for clear demonstration
const containerStyle = {
  padding: '20px',
  fontFamily: 'Arial, sans-serif',
  maxWidth: '800px',
  margin: '0 auto'
}

return (
  <div style={containerStyle}>
    <h1>🔄 React Class Lifecycle Methods</h1>
    {/* Component content */}
  </div>
)
```

### CSS Modules (Production Pattern)
For reusable components like Navigation:
- File: [src/components/Navigation/Navigation.css](mdc:src/components/Navigation/Navigation.css)
- Import: `import './Navigation.css'`
- Use class names directly: `<nav className="navigation">`

